statement:
Let P, k, j, n' ∈ ℕ, let g = (g_1, …, g_k) be an orthonormal family in ℝ^P with span G, H^k := μHE[k], let T ∈ 𝒟_j(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ j) have an integer multiplicity representation R_T = (M, θ, ξ) (IMRep univ j with R_T.Represents T), let Φ : Λ^{n'} → Λ^j be a continuous linear map and ω a test n'-form on ℝ^P (TestFormOn univ n'). Put F(t) := currentEval T (y ↦ Φ(ω(t + y))) for t ∈ ℝ^P. Then:
(i) F is continuous on ℝ^P;
(ii) F is H^k-integrable on every bounded Borel set E ⊆ G;
(iii) if moreover R_T.measure(ℝ^P ∖ G^⊥) = 0, then F is H^k-integrable on every Borel set E ⊆ G.
